4:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-03-10T02:27:56Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T11:21:16Z","closed_at":"2026-03-14T11:21:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.7.dev2, 4.6.1.stable\nNot reproducible in: 4.5.1.stable\n\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26200) - Godot v4.6.1.stable - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9159) - AMD Ryzen AI 7 H 350 w/ Radeon 860M (16 threads) - 31.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen right-clicking an existing key(suppose at time `t1`) and then left-clicking an empty space on the same track(suppose at time `t2`), and deselect the key, then select any key again, these keys visually shift by `t2-t1` during selection. When deselected, the key shifts back to its correct original time.\n\nExpected behavior: Keys should remain at their actual time positions when selected.\n\nBehavior in 4.6.1-stable:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4f3eec2-203f-4572-888d-49f3730d2db2\n\nBehavior in 4.5.1-stable:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51310874-6177-44cb-a986-bdd77ec300ab\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Right-click on an existing keyframe (suppose this is at time `t1`).\n2. Left-click on an empty position on the track of that keyframe (suppose this is at time `t2`).\n3. Left-click somewhere else in the editor to deselect the key.\n4. Select any keyframe again.\n5. The selected keys visually shift their position by `t2 - t1`. \n6. Deselect the keys, they shift back to their actual correct time.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25857694/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"no